# encoquencer: the motoquencer fader-mode-2 gate-probability plate codes (#84)
# do NOT apply to the E4. encoquencer.md "LED visualization" splits the two
# surfaces explicitly:
#
#   "The middle three LEDs below each encoder have the same function as the
#    touch button's LED in the M4: They reflect the current `buttonmode`."
#
# and gives the gate probabilities their own, different scheme in the 25-cell
# ring instead ("The eight possible settings are represented by eight positions
# in the ring. The LEDs are blue for the various standard random positions of
# 100%, 50%, 25% and 12%. The positions for playing a note every 2nd or 4th turn
# are light green. And the special position 1 ... is magenta."). The ring itself
# is panel-only and not modelled; what matters here is that the step LED keeps
# reporting the buttonmode in fader mode 2, with no blinking.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[e4]
[encoquencer]
    clock       = I1
    fadermode   = I2
    numsteps    = 4
    numfaders   = 4
    buttonmode  = 0
    defaultgate = 1
    cv          = O1
    gate        = O2
>>>
# Fader mode 2 (gate probability) and encoder 1 dialled all the way down to
# notch 1 (the conditional-random setting, which on the M4 blinks fastest).
@0 set I2 2
@1 turn E1.1 -7
# The step LEDs are the buttonmode-0 gate colour, the `buttoncolor` default 0.1
# -- not the manual's blue 1.2 -- on every gate-on step.
@2 expect E1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@2 expect E1.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@2 expect E2.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
# And they stay lit: at tick 30 every one of the M4's blink codes would be in an
# off phase, and at tick 44 all four of them are.
@30 expect E1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@30 expect E1.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@44 expect E1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@44 expect E1.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@44 expect E4.led 1 tol 1e-6
# Pushing encoder 1 still toggles its gate off (buttonmode 0 is untouched), and
# a gate-off step is dark -- the plates are reporting gates, not probabilities.
@45 push E1.1 1
@46 push E1.1 0
@46 expect E1.led 0 tol 1e-6
@46 expect E1.color 0 tol 1e-6
@46 expect E2.led 1 tol 1e-6
